From eb1da48bcb4d7e33cc86c9be32b76aab30a99ebf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 01:16:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ActiveAE: a resampler that does not open is never used, and
 the engine opens its output again

CActiveAEBufferPoolResample::ChangeResampler() dropped what
CActiveAEResampleFFMPEG::Init() returned, and Create() always said it
worked. A resampler that did not open was then used all the same: after
a failed swr_alloc_set_opts2() (FFmpeg 9 refuses a channel layout of no
channel there, and frees the context) GetBufferedSamples() went into
swr_get_delay() with a null context, a SIGSEGV on the next pass of the
engine; after a failed swr_init() (a sample rate of 0) the same call
divided by that rate; and where neither happened, each Resample() that
failed on it had the pool open it again, at every pass, with no sound.

- CActiveAEResampleFFMPEG frees the context wherever Init() fails, and
  Resample(), GetDelay() and GetBufferedSamples() do nothing without one
  (-1, 0 and 0).
- A pool says when its resampler did not open (ResamplerFailed(),
  Create() returns false, and kodi.log names both formats), and passes
  nothing on: neither resampled, nor its input as it is, which would be
  another format than the pool's. It does not try again by itself.
- CActiveAE::ResamplerFailed(), at the end of Configure() and in the
  states that run the stages, treats a pool of the sink or of a stream
  that did not open as a sink that did not open: the engine goes to
  AE_TOP_ERROR, opens its output again after the retry interval it
  already has, and makes every resampler anew. Draining before a
  reconfiguration does not wait for a pool that drains nothing.
  The player sees no sink meanwhile: it plays the video, drops the
  sound of the stream as its time comes, and if that lasts it closes the
  stream and says so on screen; without the stream the engine tries
  again at once.
- The other users of a resampler: the remapper of a stream whose
  channels are not in FFmpeg's order is left out where it does not open
  (the samples go on in the decoder's order, not as an empty packet); a
  GUI sound whose resampler does not open stays silent once, instead of
  being mixed with a count of -1; the sink's packet of silence with
  noise is plain silence instead of what av_samples_alloc() left in it;
  and paplayer fails the stream as for a format it cannot read.

A resampler that opens works as before: the same samples, byte for byte.

Reported by dangerouslaser.
